# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MasterFabric Project Tracker — environment overview
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This repo is clients only. Backend env lives in sibling repos.
#
#   masterfabric-core-base/mf-go/.env.example     →  mf-go/.env
#   masterfabric-particulars (project-tracker)    →  service / docker env
#   mf-expo/.env.example                          →  mf-expo/.env.development
#
# Optional repo root file `local.env` is loaded by mf-expo/app.config.js (overrides)
# so you can keep machine-specific GraphQL URLs outside mf-expo.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Backend (sibling repos) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# core-base mf-go: DATABASE_DSN, REDIS_*, JWT_SECRET, PARTICULAR_JWT_SECRET, …
# particulars: ./scripts/setup-project-tracker.sh — align PARTICULAR_JWT_SECRET with mf-go

# ── mf-expo (Expo app) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# See: mf-expo/.env.example
# Point GraphQL at **core-base mf-go** (auth/orgs/personal todos; org projects hop via Particular):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_GRAPHQL_URL=http://localhost:8080/graphql
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GRAPHQL_URL=http://localhost:8080/graphql
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MF_PROJECT_TRACKER_PARTICULAR=project_tracker
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MF_PARTICULAR_PORT=39205
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MF_PARTICULAR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:39205
